[2026-03-14T19:24:12.066Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NcH7VRkHvSjd1YJ9rVpHnz","type":"tool_result","content":"   500→   500→#### Test: FilterSidebar stops filter — check multiple options\n   501→   501→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   502→   502→- **Initial state**: Results page with various flights\n   503→   503→- **Action**: User checks both \"Nonstop\" and \"1 stop\" checkboxes\n   504→   504→- **Expected**: Both nonstop and 1-stop flights are displayed. Only 2+ stop flights are hidden.\n   505→   505→\n   506→   506→#### Test: FilterSidebar stops filter — uncheck to remove filter\n   507→   507→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   508→   508→- **Initial state**: \"Nonstop\" checkbox is checked, only nonstop flights shown\n   509→   509→- **Action**: User unchecks \"Nonstop\"\n   510→   510→- **Expected**: All flights are displayed again (no stops filter active).\n   511→   511→\n   512→   512→#### Test: FilterSidebar airlines filter shows airlines with flight counts\n   513→   513→- **Components**: FilterSidebar\n   514→   514→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded with results from multiple airlines\n   515→   515→- **Action**: User observes the Airlines filter section\n   516→   516→- **Expected**: A list of airline names is shown, each with a checkbox and a count of how many flights that airline has in the results (e.g., \"Delta (12)\", \"United (8)\").\n   517→   517→\n   518→   518→#### Test: FilterSidebar airlines filter — select specific airline\n   519→   519→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   520→   520→- **Initial state**: Results with flights from Delta, United, and American\n   521→   521→- **Action**: User checks the \"Delta\" checkbox in the Airlines filter\n   522→   522→- **Expected**: Only Delta flights are shown in results. United and American flights are hidden.\n   523→   523→\n   524→   524→#### Test: FilterSidebar airlines filter — select multiple airlines\n   525→   525→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   526→   526→- **Initial state**: Results with flights from multiple airlines\n   527→   527→- **Action**: User checks \"Delta\" and \"United\"\n   528→   528→- **Expected**: Only Delta and United flights are shown. Other airline flights are hidden.\n   529→   529→\n   530→   530→#### Test: FilterSidebar price range slider displays histogram\n   531→   531→- **Components**: FilterSidebar\n   532→   532→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   533→   533→- **Action**: User observes the Price range filter section\n   534→   534→- **Expected**: A price range slider is displayed with min and max handles. Above or within the slider, a histogram shows the distribution of prices across the results. The min and max price labels are shown.\n   535→   535→\n   536→   536→#### Test: FilterSidebar price range slider filters results\n   537→   537→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   538→   538→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights ranging from $150 to $800\n   539→   539→- **Action**: User drags the max price handle to $400\n   540→   540→- **Expected**: Only flights priced at $400 or below are displayed. Flights above $400 are hidden. The slider shows the updated max value.\n   541→   541→\n   542→   542→#### Test: FilterSidebar price range slider — adjust min price\n   543→   543→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   544→   544→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights ranging from $150 to $800\n   545→   545→- **Action**: User drags the min price handle to $300\n   546→   546→- **Expected**: Only flights priced at $300 or above are displayed. Flights below $300 are hidden.\n   547→   547→\n   548→   548→#### Test: FilterSidebar duration range slider filters results\n   549→   549→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   550→   550→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights of various durations\n   551→   551→- **Action**: User adjusts the duration slider to max 6 hours\n   552→   552→- **Expected**: Only flights with duration of 6 hours or less are displayed. Longer flights are hidden.\n   553→   553→\n   554→   554→#### Test: FilterSidebar departure time filter — Morning checkbox\n   555→   555→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   556→   556→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various times\n   557→   557→- **Action**: User checks \"Morning\" in the Departure time filter\n   558→   558→- **Expected**: Only flights departing in the morning time window are displayed.\n   559→   559→\n   560→   560→#### Test: FilterSidebar departure time filter — multiple time periods\n   561→   561→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   562→   562→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various times\n   563→   563→- **Action**: User checks \"Morning\" and \"Evening\"\n   564→   564→- **Expected**: Flights departing in either morning or evening time windows are displayed. Afternoon and night flights are hidden.\n   565→   565→\n   566→   566→#### Test: FilterSidebar departure time filter — arrival time checkboxes\n   567→   567→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   568→   568→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   569→   569→- **Action**: User checks \"Afternoon\" in the arrival time checkbox group\n   570→   570→- **Expected**: Only flights arriving in the afternoon are displayed.\n   571→   571→\n   572→   572→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by dropdown — default \"Best\"\n   573→   573→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   574→   574→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded, no sort selection made\n   575→   575→- **Action**: User observes the Sort by dropdown\n   576→   576→- **Expected**: The dropdown shows \"Best\" as the default selected sort option.\n   577→   577→\n   578→   578→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Price (lowest)\n   579→   579→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   580→   580→- **Initial state**: Results page with multiple flights at different prices\n   581→   581→- **Action**: User selects \"Price (lowest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   582→   582→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the cheapest flight first. Prices increase going down the list.\n   583→   583→\n   584→   584→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Duration (shortest)\n   585→   585→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   586→   586→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights of various durations\n   587→   587→- **Action**: User selects \"Duration (shortest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   588→   588→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the shortest flight first. Durations increase going down the list.\n   589→   589→\n   590→   590→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Departure time (earliest)\n   591→   591→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   592→   592→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various departure times\n   593→   593→- **Action**: User selects \"Departure time (earliest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   594→   594→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the earliest departure first.\n   595→   595→\n   596→   596→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Arrival time (earliest)\n   597→   597→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   598→   598→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various arrival times\n   599→   599→- **Action**: User selects \"Arrival time (earliest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   600→   600→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the earliest arrival first.\n   601→   601→\n   602→   602→#### Test: FilterSidebar combining multiple filters\n   603→   603→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   604→   604→- **Initial state**: Results page with diverse flights\n   605→   605→- **Action**: User checks \"Nonstop\" in Stops, selects \"Delta\" in Airlines, and sets max price to $500\n   606→   606→- **Expected**: Only nonstop Delta flights priced at $500 or below are shown. All three filters are applied simultaneously.\n   607→   607→\n   608→   608→#### Test: FilterSidebar filters can be used repeatedly\n   609→   609→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   610→   610→- **Initial state**: Results page with no filters\n   611→   611→- **Action**: User checks \"Nonstop\", observes filtered results, then unchecks \"Nonstop\" and checks \"1 stop\", then changes sort to \"Price (lowest)\"\n   612→   612→- **Expected**: Each filter change updates results correctly. The filters work properly on repeated use.\n   613→   613→\n   614→   614→### FlightResultCard\n   615→   615→\n   616→   616→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays airline info\n   617→   617→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   618→   618→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded with flights\n   619→   619→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   620→   620→- **Expected**: The card shows a colored circle with the airline's initials (airline logo) and the airline name next to it.\n   621→   621→\n   622→   622→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays departure and arrival times\n   623→   623→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   624→   624→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   625→   625→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   626→   626→- **Expected**: The card shows departure time → arrival time (e.g., \"8:00 AM → 4:30 PM\"). If the flight arrives on a different day, a \"+1\" day indicator is shown next to the arrival time.\n   627→   627→\n   628→   628→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays flight duration\n   629→   629→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   630→   630→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   631→   631→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   632→   632→- **Expected**: The card shows the total flight duration in hours and minutes format (e.g., \"5h 30m\").\n   633→   633→\n   634→   634→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays stops and layover info\n   635→   635→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   636→   636→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded with a connecting flight\n   637→   637→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card for a connecting flight\n   638→   638→- **Expected**: The card shows the number of stops and layover airport codes (e.g., \"1 stop · DFW\"). A nonstop flight shows \"Nonstop\".\n   639→   639→\n   640→   640→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays price prominently\n   641→   641→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   642→   642→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   643→   643→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   644→   644→- **Expected**: The price is displayed prominently and right-aligned on the card (e.g., \"$342\").\n   645→   645→\n   646→   646→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays CO₂ emissions\n   647→   647→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   648→   648→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   649→   649→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   650→   650→- **Expected**: A CO₂ emissions estimate is shown on the card (e.g., \"130 kg CO₂\").\n   651→   651→\n   652→   652→#### Test: FlightResultCard expand to show details\n   653→   653→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   654→   654→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded, flight card is collapsed\n   655→   655→- **Action**: User clicks on a flight result card to expand it\n   656→   656→- **Expected**: The card expands to show a detailed section including: each leg of the journey with departure/arrival times and airports, terminal info, layover duration and airport (for connecting flights), aircraft type, amenities icons (Wi-Fi, power, entertainment), and baggage allowance information.\n   657→   657→\n   658→   658→#### Test: FlightResultCard collapse details\n   659→   659→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   660→   660→- **Initial state**: A flight result card is expanded showing details\n   661→   661→- **Action**: User clicks the card again to collapse it\n   662→   662→- **Expected**: The expanded details section collapses. The card returns to its compact view.\n   663→   663→\n   664→   664→#### Test: FlightResultCard details show leg-by-leg breakdown\n   665→   665→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   666→   666→- **Initial state**: A connecting flight card is expanded\n   667→   667→- **Action**: User examines the expanded details\n   668→   668→- **Expected**: Each leg is shown separately with: departure time and airport (with terminal), arrival time and airport (with terminal), flight number, and duration. Between legs, the layover duration and airport are displayed.\n   669→   669→\n   670→   670→#### Test: FlightResultCard details show amenities icons\n   671→   671→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   672→   672→- **Initial state**: A flight card is expanded showing details\n   673→   673→- **Action**: User examines the amenities section\n   674→   674→- **Expected**: Icons for available amenities are shown: Wi-Fi icon (if has_wifi), power outlet icon (if has_power), entertainment icon (if has_entertainment). Only available amenities are shown or unavailable ones are visually muted.\n   675→   675→\n   676→   676→#### Test: FlightResultCard details show baggage allowance\n   677→   677→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   678→   678→- **Initial state**: A flight card is expanded showing details\n   679→   679→- **Action**: User examines the baggage section\n   680→   680→- **Expected**: Baggage allowance information is displayed in the expanded details.\n   681→   681→\n   682→   682→#### Test: FlightResultCard overnight flight shows +1 day indicator\n   683→   683→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   684→   684→- **Initial state**: Results include an overnight flight (e.g., departs 11:00 PM, arrives 6:00 AM next day)\n   685→   685→- **Action**: User observes the overnight flight card\n   686→   686→- **Expected**: The arrival time shows a \"+1\" indicator next to it (e.g., \"6:00 AM +1\") to indicate arrival on the next day.\n   687→   687→\n   688→   688→#### Test: FlightResultCard clicking \"Select\" navigates to booking page\n   689→   689→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   690→   690→- **Initial state**: Results page with flight cards, a card is expanded\n   691→   691→- **Action**: User clicks the select/book button on a flight card\n   692→   692→- **Expected**: The app navigates to the Flight Details / Booking page with the selected flight's information.\n   693→   693→\n   694→   694→#### Test: FlightResultCard expand and collapse multiple cards\n   695→   695→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   696→   696→- **Initial state**: Results page with multiple flight cards\n   697→   697→- **Action**: User expands card A, then expands card B, then collapses card A\n   698→   698→- **Expected**: Each card independently expands and collapses. Card B remains expanded when card A is collapsed.\n   699→   699→\n   700→   700→### TrackPricesToggle\n   701→   701→\n   702→   702→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle is displayed on results page\n   703→   703→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle\n   704→   704→- **Initial state**: Search results page loaded\n   705→   705→- **Action**: User observes the track prices control\n   706→   706→- **Expected**: A \"Track prices\" toggle button is visible on the results page. It is initially in the off/untracked state.\n   707→   707→\n   708→   708→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle enables price tracking\n   709→   709→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle\n   710→   710→- **Initial state**: Results page for LAX → JFK, Mar 25 – Apr 1, toggle is off\n   711→   711→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Track prices\" toggle\n   712→   712→- **Expected**: The toggle switches to the on/tracked state with a visual indicator (e.g., filled toggle, checkmark, or color change). The route is saved to tracked_routes in the database for the current session.\n   713→   713→\n   714→   714→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle disables price tracking\n   715→   715→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle\n   716→   716→- **Initial state**: Price tracking is enabled (toggle is on) for the current route\n   717→   717→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Track prices\" toggle again\n   718→   718→- **Expected**: The toggle switches to the off/untracked state. The route is removed from tracked_routes in the database.\n   719→   719→\n   720→   720→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle reflects existing tracked route\n   721→   721→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle\n   722→   722→- **Initial state**: User previously tracked LAX → JFK route, then searches LAX → JFK again\n   723→   723→- **Action**: User observes the toggle on the results page\n   724→   724→- **Expected**: The toggle is in the on/tracked state, reflecting that this route is already being tracked.\n   725→   725→\n   726→   726→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle tracked route appears in My Trips\n   727→   727→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle, TrackedRouteCard\n   728→   728→- **Initial state**: User enables price tracking for LAX → JFK\n   729→   729→- **Action**: User navigates to My Trips page and selects the \"Tracked\" tab\n   730→   730→- **Expected**: The tracked route (LAX → JFK) appears in the Tracked tab with route details, date range, current lowest price, and untrack button.\n   731→   731→\n   732→   732→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle can be toggled multiple times\n   733→   733→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle\n   734→   734→- **Initial state**: Results page, toggle is off\n   735→   735→- **Action**: User toggles on, interacts with filters, toggles off, then toggles on again\n   736→   736→- **Expected**: Each toggle correctly switches state. The database is updated on each toggle. The final state is tracked (on).\n   737→   737→\n   738→   738→### Pagination\n   739→   739→\n   740→   740→#### Test: Pagination \"Load more\" button is displayed at bottom of results\n   741→   741→- **Components**: Pagination\n   742→   742→- **Initial state**: Search results page with more results available than initially displayed\n   743→   743→- **Action**: User scrolls to the bottom of the results list\n   744→   744→- **Expected**: A \"Load more results\" button is visible at the bottom of the results list.\n   745→   745→\n   746→   746→#### Test: Pagination loading more results appends to list\n   747→   747→- **Components**: Pagination, FlightResultCard\n   748→   748→- **Initial state**: Results page showing initial set of results (e.g., 20 flights), more available\n   749→   749→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Load more results\" button\n   750→   750→- **Expected**: Additional flight results are appended below the existing results. The previously displayed results remain in place. The new results are visible.\n   751→   751→\n   752→   752→#### Test: Pagination button hidden when all results loaded\n   753→   753→- **Components**: Pagination\n   754→   754→- **Initial state**: All available flight results have been loaded\n   755→   755→- **Action**: User scrolls to the bottom of the results list\n   756→   756→- **Expected**: The \"Load more results\" button is no longer displayed (or is disabled) since there are no more results to load.\n   757→   757→\n   758→   758→#### Test: Pagination shows loading state while fetching\n   759→   759→- **Components**: Pagination\n   760→   760→- **Initial state**: Results page with more results available\n   761→   761→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Load more results\" button\n   762→   762→- **Expected**: The button shows a loading indicator (spinner or \"Loading...\" text) while additional results are being fetched. The button is not clickable during loading.\n   763→   763→\n   764→   764→#### Test: Pagination preserves filters when loading more\n   765→   765→- **Components**: Pagination, FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   766→   766→- **Initial state**: Results page with \"Nonstop\" filter active, showing filtered results\n   767→   767→- **Action**: User clicks \"Load more results\"\n   768→   768→- **Expected**: The newly loaded results also respect the active filters. Only nonstop flights are appended.\n   769→   769→\n   770→   770→#### Test: Pagination can be used repeatedly\n   771→   771→- **Components**: Pagination, FlightResultCard\n   772→   772→- **Initial state**: Results page with many available results\n   773→   773→- **Action**: User clicks \"Load more\" three times in sequence\n   774→   774→- **Expected**: Each click appends more results. Results accumulate correctly without duplicates. The button disappears when no more results remain.\n   775→   775→\n   776→   776→## Page: Flight Details / Booking\n   777→   777→\n   778→   778→### Components\n   779→   779→- FlightSummary\n   780→   780→- PriceBreakdown\n   781→   781→- PassengerForm\n   782→   782→- BookingAction\n   783→   783→\n   784→   784→### FlightSummary\n   785→   785→\n   786→   786→#### Test: FlightSummary displays full outbound itinerary\n   787→   787→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   788→   788→- **Initial state**: User selected a one-way flight (LAX → JFK, nonstop, 5h 30m, Delta DL100) from search results\n   789→   789→- **Action**: User observes the Flight Details / Booking page\n   790→   790→- **Expected**: The FlightSummary shows the outbound itinerary with airline name and logo (colored circle with \"DL\" initials), flight number \"DL100\", departure airport \"LAX\" with terminal info, arrival airport \"JFK\" with terminal info, departure time, arrival time, and total duration \"5h 30m\". A timeline visualization connects departure and arrival.\n   791→   791→\n   792→   792→#### Test: FlightSummary displays outbound and return flights for round trip\n   793→   793→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   794→   794→- **Initial state**: User selected a round-trip flight (LAX → JFK outbound, JFK → LAX return) from search results\n   795→   795→- **Action**: User observes the FlightSummary section\n   796→   796→- **Expected**: Two separate flight sections are displayed — one labeled for the outbound journey (LAX → JFK) and one for the return journey (JFK → LAX). Each section shows its own airline, flight number, times, duration, and timeline visualization.\n   797→   797→\n   798→   798→#### Test: FlightSummary displays connecting flight with multiple legs\n   799→   799→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   800→   800→- **Initial state**: User selected a connecting flight (LAX → DFW → JFK, 1 stop) from search results\n   801→   801→- **Action**: User observes the FlightSummary section\n   802→   802→- **Expected**: The itinerary displays both legs in order: Leg 1 (LAX → DFW) with its airline, flight number, departure/arrival times, terminal info, and duration; then a layover indicator showing layover duration and airport (e.g., \"2h 15m layover at DFW\"); then Leg 2 (DFW → JFK) with its details. The timeline visualization shows the full journey with the layover marked.\n   803→   803→\n   804→   804→#### Test: FlightSummary shows total duration and stops count\n   805→   805→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   806→   806→- **Initial state**: User selected a 1-stop flight with total duration 8h 45m\n   807→   807→- **Action**: User observes the FlightSummary header area\n   808→   808→- **Expected**: A summary line displays the total journey duration \"8h 45m\" and the number of stops \"1 stop\". For nonstop flights, it shows \"Nonstop\".\n   809→   809→\n   810→   810→#### Test: FlightSummary shows overnight arrival indicator\n   811→   811→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   812→   812→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight that arrives the next day (departs 11:00 PM, arrives 6:00 AM +1)\n   813→   813→- **Action**: User observes the arrival time in FlightSummary\n   814→   814→- **Expected**: The arrival time displays a \"+1\" indicator next to it, signaling the flight arrives the following day.\n   815→   815→\n   816→   816→#### Test: FlightSummary shows aircraft type and amenities\n   817→   817→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   818→   818→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight with aircraft_type \"Boeing 737-800\", has_wifi=true, has_power=true, has_entertainment=false\n   819→   819→- **Action**: User observes the flight leg details in FlightSummary\n   820→   820→- **Expected**: The aircraft type \"Boeing 737-800\" is displayed. Amenity icons are shown: Wi-Fi icon (present), power outlet icon (present). Entertainment icon is not shown or shown as unavailable.\n   821→   821→\n   822→   822→#### Test: FlightSummary shows baggage allowance\n   823→   823→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   824→   824→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight and the booking page is loaded\n   825→   825→- **Action**: User observes the FlightSummary details\n   826→   826→- **Expected**: Baggage allowance information is displayed for the selected cabin class (e.g., \"1 carry-on bag, 1 checked bag included\" for economy).\n   827→   827→\n   828→   828→### PriceBreakdown\n   829→   829→\n   830→   830→#### Test: PriceBreakdown displays base fare per passenger\n   831→   831→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   832→   832→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight for 1 adult in economy class, base fare $250, taxes $45\n   833→   833→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   834→   834→- **Expected**: The breakdown shows a line item \"Base fare\" with \"$250\" for 1 adult. The line item is labeled with the passenger type \"Adult × 1\".\n   835→   835→\n   836→   836→#### Test: PriceBreakdown displays taxes and fees\n   837→   837→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   838→   838→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight with taxes_cents = 4500\n   839→   839→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   840→   840→- **Expected**: A \"Taxes and fees\" line item shows \"$45.00\". The taxes are listed as a separate line from the base fare.\n   841→   841→\n   842→   842→#### Test: PriceBreakdown displays total price\n   843→   843→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   844→   844→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight with base fare $250 and taxes $45\n   845→   845→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   846→   846→- **Expected**: A prominently displayed \"Total\" line shows \"$295.00\". It is visually distinct (bold, larger font, or separated by a divider) from the individual line items.\n   847→   847→\n   848→   848→#### Test: PriceBreakdown shows per-passenger-type pricing for mixed group\n   849→   849→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   850→   850→- **Initial state**: User searched with 2 adults, 1 child, 1 infant and selected a flight\n   851→   851→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   852→   852→- **Expected**: The breakdown shows separate line items for each passenger type: \"Adult × 2\" with the per-adult base fare and subtotal, \"Child × 1\" with the child base fare, \"Infant × 1\" with the infant base fare. Taxes and fees are shown. The grand total sums all passengers.\n   853→   853→\n   854→   854→#### Test: PriceBreakdown updates for round-trip flights\n   855→   855→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   856→   856→- **Initial state**: User selected a round-trip flight (outbound + return)\n   857→   857→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   858→   858→- **Expected**: The breakdown includes pricing for both the outbound and return flights. The total reflects the combined cost of both directions plus all taxes and fees.\n   859→   859→\n   860→   860→#### Test: PriceBreakdown reflects selected cabin class pricing\n   861→   861→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   862→   862→- **Initial state**: User searched for Business class and selected a flight\n   863→   863→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   864→   864→- **Expected**: The cabin class \"Business\" is indicated in the breakdown. The base fare reflects the business class pricing (higher than economy). The total price matches the business class total_price_cents from the database.\n   865→   865→\n   866→   866→### PassengerForm\n   867→   867→\n   868→   868→#### Test: PassengerForm displays correct number of passenger forms\n   869→   869→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   870→   870→- **Initial state**: User searched with 2 adults and 1 child, then selected a flight\n   871→   871→- **Action**: User observes the PassengerForm section\n   872→   872→- **Expected**: Three separate passenger sub-forms are displayed, labeled \"Passenger 1 (Adult)\", \"Passenger 2 (Adult)\", and \"Passenger 3 (Child)\". Each form has fields for first name, last name, date of birth, and gender.\n   873→   873→\n   874→   874→#### Test: PassengerForm shows primary passenger contact fields\n   875→   875→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   876→   876→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded with 2 adults\n   877→   877→- **Action**: User observes Passenger 1 form\n   878→   878→- **Expected**: Passenger 1 (primary passenger) has additional fields for email address and phone number that are not present on the other passenger forms.\n   879→   879→\n   880→   880→#### Test: PassengerForm first name and last name input\n   881→   881→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   882→   882→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, passenger forms are empty\n   883→   883→- **Action**: User types \"John\" in the first name field and \"Doe\" in the last name field of Passenger 1\n   884→   884→- **Expected**: The first name field displays \"John\" and the last name field displays \"Doe\". The input is reflected in the form state.\n   885→   885→\n   886→   886→#### Test: PassengerForm date of birth picker\n   887→   887→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   888→   888→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   889→   889→- **Action**: User clicks the date of birth field and selects a date (e.g., January 15, 1990)\n   890→   890→- **Expected**: A date picker opens. After selecting the date, the field displays \"01/15/1990\" (or equivalent formatted date). The date picker closes.\n   891→   891→\n   892→   892→#### Test: PassengerForm gender dropdown\n   893→   893→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   894→   894→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   895→   895→- **Action**: User clicks the gender dropdown\n   896→   896→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens with options (e.g., \"Male\", \"Female\", \"Other\", \"Prefer not to say\"). Selecting an option updates the field and closes the dropdown.\n   897→   897→\n   898→   898→#### Test: PassengerForm email validation\n   899→   899→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   900→   900→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   901→   901→- **Action**: User types \"invalid-email\" in the email field and attempts to submit\n   902→   902→- **Expected**: A validation error appears on the email field indicating an invalid email format (e.g., \"Please enter a valid email address\"). The form does not submit.\n   903→   903→\n   904→   904→#### Test: PassengerForm email accepts valid input\n   905→   905→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   906→   906→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   907→   907→- **Action**: User types \"john.doe@example.com\" in the email field\n   908→   908→- **Expected**: The email field displays \"john.doe@example.com\" with no validation errors.\n   909→   909→\n   910→   910→#### Test: PassengerForm phone number input\n   911→   911→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   912→   912→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   913→   913→- **Action**: User types \"+1 555-123-4567\" in the phone number field\n   914→   914→- **Expected**: The phone number field accepts and displays the input. No validation error is shown.\n   915→   915→\n   916→   916→#### Test: PassengerForm required field validation\n   917→   917→- **Components**: PassengerForm, BookingAction\n   918→   918→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, all passenger forms are empty\n   919→   919→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Book Flight\" button without filling in any fields\n   920→   920→- **Expected**: Validation errors appear on all required fields (first name, last name, date of birth, gender for each passenger; email and phone for primary passenger). The booking is not submitted. Error messages indicate which fields are required.\n   921→   921→\n   922→   922→#### Test: PassengerForm infant passenger form\n   923→   923→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   924→   924→- **Initial state**: User searched with 1 adult, 1 infant and selected a flight\n   925→   925→- **Action**: User observes the passenger forms\n   926→   926→- **Expected**: Two forms are displayed: \"Passenger 1 (Adult)\" with contact fields, and \"Passenger 2 (Infant)\" with first name, last name, date of birth, and gender but no email/phone fields.\n   927→   927→\n   928→   928→#### Test: PassengerForm can be filled and edited multiple times\n   929→   929→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   930→   930→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, passenger form is empty\n   931→   931→- **Action**: User fills in first name \"John\", then changes it to \"Jane\", interacts with date of birth picker, then returns to first name and changes it to \"Alex\"\n   932→   932→- **Expected**: Each edit is correctly reflected in the form. The final state shows \"Alex\" in the first name field. Other fields retain their entered values between edits.\n   933→   933→\n   934→   934→### BookingAction\n   935→   935→\n   936→   936→#### Test: BookingAction displays \"Book Flight\" button\n   937→   937→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   938→   938→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded with flight selected\n   939→   939→- **Action**: User observes the BookingAction section\n   940→   940→- **Expected**: A prominent \"Book Flight\" button is displayed. The button text reads \"Book Flight\" and is styled as a primary action button (blue background, white text).\n   941→   941→\n   942→   942→#### Test: BookingAction successfully books a flight\n   943→   943→- **Components**: BookingAction, PassengerForm, PriceBreakdown\n   944→   944→- **Initial state**: All passenger forms are filled out correctly (Passenger 1: John Doe, john@example.com, +1 555-123-4567, DOB 1990-01-15, Male)\n   945→   945→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Book Flight\" button\n   946→   946→- **Expected**: The booking is saved to the database. A confirmation message is displayed with a unique booking reference number (e.g., \"Booking confirmed! Reference: ABC123\"). The bookings table has a new row with status \"confirmed\", the correct flight_id, session_id, cabin_class, and total_price_cents. The booking_passengers table has corresponding passenger records.\n   947→   947→\n   948→   948→#### Test: BookingAction shows booking reference number\n   949→   949→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   950→   950→- **Initial state**: User has just successfully booked a flight\n   951→   951→- **Action**: User observes the confirmation\n   952→   952→- **Expected**: A booking reference number is prominently displayed (e.g., \"Your booking reference: GF-ABC123\"). The reference is unique and can be used to identify the booking in the My Trips page.\n   953→   953→\n   954→   954→#### Test: BookingAction prevents double booking\n   955→   955→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   956→   956→- **Initial state**: User has just successfully booked a flight and sees the confirmation\n   957→   957→- **Action**: User attempts to click \"Book Flight\" again (e.g., via browser back or re-clicking)\n   958→   958→- **Expected**: The button is either disabled after successful booking, or the system prevents duplicate bookings. No second booking is created in the database.\n   959→   959→\n   960→   960→#### Test: BookingAction shows loading state during submission\n   961→   961→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   962→   962→- **Initial state**: All passenger forms filled, user clicks \"Book Flight\"\n   963→   963→- **Action**: User observes the button during submission\n   964→   964→- **Expected**: The button shows a loading indicator (spinner or \"Booking...\" text) while the request is being processed. The button is disabled during this time to prevent multiple clicks.\n   965→   965→\n   966→   966→#### Test: BookingAction booking appears in My Trips\n   967→   967→- **Components**: BookingAction, TripCard\n   968→   968→- **Initial state**: User has just successfully booked a flight (LAX → JFK, Mar 25, Delta DL100, $295)\n   969→   969→- **Action**: User navigates to the My Trips page\n   970→   970→- **Expected**: The \"Upcoming\" tab shows the newly booked trip with route \"LAX → JFK\", date \"Mar 25\", airline \"Delta\", status badge \"Confirmed\", price \"$295\", and the booking reference number.\n   971→   971→\n   972→   972→#### Test: BookingAction handles booking error gracefully\n   973→   973→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   974→   974→- **Initial state**: All passenger forms filled, but a network or server error occurs during booking\n   975→   975→- **Action**: User clicks \"Book Flight\" and the request fails\n   976→   976→- **Expected**: An error message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking failed. Please try again.\"). The form data is preserved so the user does not need to re-enter information. The \"Book Flight\" button becomes clickable again.\n   977→   977→\n   978→   978→## Page: My Trips\n   979→   979→\n   980→   980→### Components\n   981→   981→- TripsTabs\n   982→   982→- TripCard\n   983→   983→- TrackedRouteCard\n   984→   984→- CancelBookingModal\n   985→   985→\n   986→   986→### TripsTabs\n   987→   987→\n   988→   988→#### Test: TripsTabs displays three tabs\n   989→   989→- **Components**: TripsTabs\n   990→   990→- **Initial state**: User navigates to the My Trips page\n   991→   991→- **Action**: User observes the tab bar at the top of the page\n   992→   992→- **Expected**: Three tabs are displayed: \"Upcoming\", \"Past\", and \"Tracked\". The \"Upcoming\" tab is selected by default and visually highlighted (e.g., underline or bold text with primary color #1A73E8).\n   993→   993→\n   994→   994→#### Test: TripsTabs switches to Past tab\n   995→   995→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TripCard\n   996→   996→- **Initial state**: My Trips page loaded with \"Upcoming\" tab active, user has both upcoming and past bookings\n   997→   997→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Past\" tab\n   998→   998→- **Expected**: The \"Past\" tab becomes visually selected. The content area updates to show only trips with past departure dates (status \"Completed\" or \"Cancelled\"). Upcoming trips are no longer visible.\n   999→   999→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d1a1082-0764-4fd1-bb12-0bb26acd7c93","uuid":"ba27c87e-4cd5-474e-b163-f8321e2c391b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/agent/.claude/projects/-repo/1d1a1082-0764-4fd1-bb12-0bb26acd7c93/tool-results/toolu_01WdkqW3SpBmCBdtnNee6vsW.txt","content":"   500→#### Test: FilterSidebar stops filter — check multiple options\n   501→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   502→- **Initial state**: Results page with various flights\n   503→- **Action**: User checks both \"Nonstop\" and \"1 stop\" checkboxes\n   504→- **Expected**: Both nonstop and 1-stop flights are displayed. Only 2+ stop flights are hidden.\n   505→\n   506→#### Test: FilterSidebar stops filter — uncheck to remove filter\n   507→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   508→- **Initial state**: \"Nonstop\" checkbox is checked, only nonstop flights shown\n   509→- **Action**: User unchecks \"Nonstop\"\n   510→- **Expected**: All flights are displayed again (no stops filter active).\n   511→\n   512→#### Test: FilterSidebar airlines filter shows airlines with flight counts\n   513→- **Components**: FilterSidebar\n   514→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded with results from multiple airlines\n   515→- **Action**: User observes the Airlines filter section\n   516→- **Expected**: A list of airline names is shown, each with a checkbox and a count of how many flights that airline has in the results (e.g., \"Delta (12)\", \"United (8)\").\n   517→\n   518→#### Test: FilterSidebar airlines filter — select specific airline\n   519→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   520→- **Initial state**: Results with flights from Delta, United, and American\n   521→- **Action**: User checks the \"Delta\" checkbox in the Airlines filter\n   522→- **Expected**: Only Delta flights are shown in results. United and American flights are hidden.\n   523→\n   524→#### Test: FilterSidebar airlines filter — select multiple airlines\n   525→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   526→- **Initial state**: Results with flights from multiple airlines\n   527→- **Action**: User checks \"Delta\" and \"United\"\n   528→- **Expected**: Only Delta and United flights are shown. Other airline flights are hidden.\n   529→\n   530→#### Test: FilterSidebar price range slider displays histogram\n   531→- **Components**: FilterSidebar\n   532→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   533→- **Action**: User observes the Price range filter section\n   534→- **Expected**: A price range slider is displayed with min and max handles. Above or within the slider, a histogram shows the distribution of prices across the results. The min and max price labels are shown.\n   535→\n   536→#### Test: FilterSidebar price range slider filters results\n   537→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   538→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights ranging from $150 to $800\n   539→- **Action**: User drags the max price handle to $400\n   540→- **Expected**: Only flights priced at $400 or below are displayed. Flights above $400 are hidden. The slider shows the updated max value.\n   541→\n   542→#### Test: FilterSidebar price range slider — adjust min price\n   543→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   544→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights ranging from $150 to $800\n   545→- **Action**: User drags the min price handle to $300\n   546→- **Expected**: Only flights priced at $300 or above are displayed. Flights below $300 are hidden.\n   547→\n   548→#### Test: FilterSidebar duration range slider filters results\n   549→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   550→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights of various durations\n   551→- **Action**: User adjusts the duration slider to max 6 hours\n   552→- **Expected**: Only flights with duration of 6 hours or less are displayed. Longer flights are hidden.\n   553→\n   554→#### Test: FilterSidebar departure time filter — Morning checkbox\n   555→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   556→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various times\n   557→- **Action**: User checks \"Morning\" in the Departure time filter\n   558→- **Expected**: Only flights departing in the morning time window are displayed.\n   559→\n   560→#### Test: FilterSidebar departure time filter — multiple time periods\n   561→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   562→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various times\n   563→- **Action**: User checks \"Morning\" and \"Evening\"\n   564→- **Expected**: Flights departing in either morning or evening time windows are displayed. Afternoon and night flights are hidden.\n   565→\n   566→#### Test: FilterSidebar departure time filter — arrival time checkboxes\n   567→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   568→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   569→- **Action**: User checks \"Afternoon\" in the arrival time checkbox group\n   570→- **Expected**: Only flights arriving in the afternoon are displayed.\n   571→\n   572→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by dropdown — default \"Best\"\n   573→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   574→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded, no sort selection made\n   575→- **Action**: User observes the Sort by dropdown\n   576→- **Expected**: The dropdown shows \"Best\" as the default selected sort option.\n   577→\n   578→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Price (lowest)\n   579→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   580→- **Initial state**: Results page with multiple flights at different prices\n   581→- **Action**: User selects \"Price (lowest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   582→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the cheapest flight first. Prices increase going down the list.\n   583→\n   584→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Duration (shortest)\n   585→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   586→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights of various durations\n   587→- **Action**: User selects \"Duration (shortest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   588→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the shortest flight first. Durations increase going down the list.\n   589→\n   590→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Departure time (earliest)\n   591→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   592→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various departure times\n   593→- **Action**: User selects \"Departure time (earliest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   594→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the earliest departure first.\n   595→\n   596→#### Test: FilterSidebar sort by Arrival time (earliest)\n   597→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   598→- **Initial state**: Results page with flights at various arrival times\n   599→- **Action**: User selects \"Arrival time (earliest)\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   600→- **Expected**: Results are reordered with the earliest arrival first.\n   601→\n   602→#### Test: FilterSidebar combining multiple filters\n   603→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   604→- **Initial state**: Results page with diverse flights\n   605→- **Action**: User checks \"Nonstop\" in Stops, selects \"Delta\" in Airlines, and sets max price to $500\n   606→- **Expected**: Only nonstop Delta flights priced at $500 or below are shown. All three filters are applied simultaneously.\n   607→\n   608→#### Test: FilterSidebar filters can be used repeatedly\n   609→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   610→- **Initial state**: Results page with no filters\n   611→- **Action**: User checks \"Nonstop\", observes filtered results, then unchecks \"Nonstop\" and checks \"1 stop\", then changes sort to \"Price (lowest)\"\n   612→- **Expected**: Each filter change updates results correctly. The filters work properly on repeated use.\n   613→\n   614→### FlightResultCard\n   615→\n   616→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays airline info\n   617→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   618→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded with flights\n   619→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   620→- **Expected**: The card shows a colored circle with the airline's initials (airline logo) and the airline name next to it.\n   621→\n   622→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays departure and arrival times\n   623→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   624→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   625→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   626→- **Expected**: The card shows departure time → arrival time (e.g., \"8:00 AM → 4:30 PM\"). If the flight arrives on a different day, a \"+1\" day indicator is shown next to the arrival time.\n   627→\n   628→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays flight duration\n   629→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   630→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   631→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   632→- **Expected**: The card shows the total flight duration in hours and minutes format (e.g., \"5h 30m\").\n   633→\n   634→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays stops and layover info\n   635→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   636→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded with a connecting flight\n   637→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card for a connecting flight\n   638→- **Expected**: The card shows the number of stops and layover airport codes (e.g., \"1 stop · DFW\"). A nonstop flight shows \"Nonstop\".\n   639→\n   640→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays price prominently\n   641→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   642→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   643→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   644→- **Expected**: The price is displayed prominently and right-aligned on the card (e.g., \"$342\").\n   645→\n   646→#### Test: FlightResultCard displays CO₂ emissions\n   647→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   648→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded\n   649→- **Action**: User observes a flight result card\n   650→- **Expected**: A CO₂ emissions estimate is shown on the card (e.g., \"130 kg CO₂\").\n   651→\n   652→#### Test: FlightResultCard expand to show details\n   653→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   654→- **Initial state**: Results page loaded, flight card is collapsed\n   655→- **Action**: User clicks on a flight result card to expand it\n   656→- **Expected**: The card expands to show a detailed section including: each leg of the journey with departure/arrival times and airports, terminal info, layover duration and airport (for connecting flights), aircraft type, amenities icons (Wi-Fi, power, entertainment), and baggage allowance information.\n   657→\n   658→#### Test: FlightResultCard collapse details\n   659→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   660→- **Initial state**: A flight result card is expanded showing details\n   661→- **Action**: User clicks the card again to collapse it\n   662→- **Expected**: The expanded details section collapses. The card returns to its compact view.\n   663→\n   664→#### Test: FlightResultCard details show leg-by-leg breakdown\n   665→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   666→- **Initial state**: A connecting flight card is expanded\n   667→- **Action**: User examines the expanded details\n   668→- **Expected**: Each leg is shown separately with: departure time and airport (with terminal), arrival time and airport (with terminal), flight number, and duration. Between legs, the layover duration and airport are displayed.\n   669→\n   670→#### Test: FlightResultCard details show amenities icons\n   671→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   672→- **Initial state**: A flight card is expanded showing details\n   673→- **Action**: User examines the amenities section\n   674→- **Expected**: Icons for available amenities are shown: Wi-Fi icon (if has_wifi), power outlet icon (if has_power), entertainment icon (if has_entertainment). Only available amenities are shown or unavailable ones are visually muted.\n   675→\n   676→#### Test: FlightResultCard details show baggage allowance\n   677→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   678→- **Initial state**: A flight card is expanded showing details\n   679→- **Action**: User examines the baggage section\n   680→- **Expected**: Baggage allowance information is displayed in the expanded details.\n   681→\n   682→#### Test: FlightResultCard overnight flight shows +1 day indicator\n   683→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   684→- **Initial state**: Results include an overnight flight (e.g., departs 11:00 PM, arrives 6:00 AM next day)\n   685→- **Action**: User observes the overnight flight card\n   686→- **Expected**: The arrival time shows a \"+1\" indicator next to it (e.g., \"6:00 AM +1\") to indicate arrival on the next day.\n   687→\n   688→#### Test: FlightResultCard clicking \"Select\" navigates to booking page\n   689→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   690→- **Initial state**: Results page with flight cards, a card is expanded\n   691→- **Action**: User clicks the select/book button on a flight card\n   692→- **Expected**: The app navigates to the Flight Details / Booking page with the selected flight's information.\n   693→\n   694→#### Test: FlightResultCard expand and collapse multiple cards\n   695→- **Components**: FlightResultCard\n   696→- **Initial state**: Results page with multiple flight cards\n   697→- **Action**: User expands card A, then expands card B, then collapses card A\n   698→- **Expected**: Each card independently expands and collapses. Card B remains expanded when card A is collapsed.\n   699→\n   700→### TrackPricesToggle\n   701→\n   702→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle is displayed on results page\n   703→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle\n   704→- **Initial state**: Search results page loaded\n   705→- **Action**: User observes the track prices control\n   706→- **Expected**: A \"Track prices\" toggle button is visible on the results page. It is initially in the off/untracked state.\n   707→\n   708→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle enables price tracking\n   709→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle\n   710→- **Initial state**: Results page for LAX → JFK, Mar 25 – Apr 1, toggle is off\n   711→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Track prices\" toggle\n   712→- **Expected**: The toggle switches to the on/tracked state with a visual indicator (e.g., filled toggle, checkmark, or color change). The route is saved to tracked_routes in the database for the current session.\n   713→\n   714→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle disables price tracking\n   715→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle\n   716→- **Initial state**: Price tracking is enabled (toggle is on) for the current route\n   717→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Track prices\" toggle again\n   718→- **Expected**: The toggle switches to the off/untracked state. The route is removed from tracked_routes in the database.\n   719→\n   720→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle reflects existing tracked route\n   721→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle\n   722→- **Initial state**: User previously tracked LAX → JFK route, then searches LAX → JFK again\n   723→- **Action**: User observes the toggle on the results page\n   724→- **Expected**: The toggle is in the on/tracked state, reflecting that this route is already being tracked.\n   725→\n   726→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle tracked route appears in My Trips\n   727→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle, TrackedRouteCard\n   728→- **Initial state**: User enables price tracking for LAX → JFK\n   729→- **Action**: User navigates to My Trips page and selects the \"Tracked\" tab\n   730→- **Expected**: The tracked route (LAX → JFK) appears in the Tracked tab with route details, date range, current lowest price, and untrack button.\n   731→\n   732→#### Test: TrackPricesToggle can be toggled multiple times\n   733→- **Components**: TrackPricesToggle\n   734→- **Initial state**: Results page, toggle is off\n   735→- **Action**: User toggles on, interacts with filters, toggles off, then toggles on again\n   736→- **Expected**: Each toggle correctly switches state. The database is updated on each toggle. The final state is tracked (on).\n   737→\n   738→### Pagination\n   739→\n   740→#### Test: Pagination \"Load more\" button is displayed at bottom of results\n   741→- **Components**: Pagination\n   742→- **Initial state**: Search results page with more results available than initially displayed\n   743→- **Action**: User scrolls to the bottom of the results list\n   744→- **Expected**: A \"Load more results\" button is visible at the bottom of the results list.\n   745→\n   746→#### Test: Pagination loading more results appends to list\n   747→- **Components**: Pagination, FlightResultCard\n   748→- **Initial state**: Results page showing initial set of results (e.g., 20 flights), more available\n   749→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Load more results\" button\n   750→- **Expected**: Additional flight results are appended below the existing results. The previously displayed results remain in place. The new results are visible.\n   751→\n   752→#### Test: Pagination button hidden when all results loaded\n   753→- **Components**: Pagination\n   754→- **Initial state**: All available flight results have been loaded\n   755→- **Action**: User scrolls to the bottom of the results list\n   756→- **Expected**: The \"Load more results\" button is no longer displayed (or is disabled) since there are no more results to load.\n   757→\n   758→#### Test: Pagination shows loading state while fetching\n   759→- **Components**: Pagination\n   760→- **Initial state**: Results page with more results available\n   761→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Load more results\" button\n   762→- **Expected**: The button shows a loading indicator (spinner or \"Loading...\" text) while additional results are being fetched. The button is not clickable during loading.\n   763→\n   764→#### Test: Pagination preserves filters when loading more\n   765→- **Components**: Pagination, FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   766→- **Initial state**: Results page with \"Nonstop\" filter active, showing filtered results\n   767→- **Action**: User clicks \"Load more results\"\n   768→- **Expected**: The newly loaded results also respect the active filters. Only nonstop flights are appended.\n   769→\n   770→#### Test: Pagination can be used repeatedly\n   771→- **Components**: Pagination, FlightResultCard\n   772→- **Initial state**: Results page with many available results\n   773→- **Action**: User clicks \"Load more\" three times in sequence\n   774→- **Expected**: Each click appends more results. Results accumulate correctly without duplicates. The button disappears when no more results remain.\n   775→\n   776→## Page: Flight Details / Booking\n   777→\n   778→### Components\n   779→- FlightSummary\n   780→- PriceBreakdown\n   781→- PassengerForm\n   782→- BookingAction\n   783→\n   784→### FlightSummary\n   785→\n   786→#### Test: FlightSummary displays full outbound itinerary\n   787→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   788→- **Initial state**: User selected a one-way flight (LAX → JFK, nonstop, 5h 30m, Delta DL100) from search results\n   789→- **Action**: User observes the Flight Details / Booking page\n   790→- **Expected**: The FlightSummary shows the outbound itinerary with airline name and logo (colored circle with \"DL\" initials), flight number \"DL100\", departure airport \"LAX\" with terminal info, arrival airport \"JFK\" with terminal info, departure time, arrival time, and total duration \"5h 30m\". A timeline visualization connects departure and arrival.\n   791→\n   792→#### Test: FlightSummary displays outbound and return flights for round trip\n   793→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   794→- **Initial state**: User selected a round-trip flight (LAX → JFK outbound, JFK → LAX return) from search results\n   795→- **Action**: User observes the FlightSummary section\n   796→- **Expected**: Two separate flight sections are displayed — one labeled for the outbound journey (LAX → JFK) and one for the return journey (JFK → LAX). Each section shows its own airline, flight number, times, duration, and timeline visualization.\n   797→\n   798→#### Test: FlightSummary displays connecting flight with multiple legs\n   799→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   800→- **Initial state**: User selected a connecting flight (LAX → DFW → JFK, 1 stop) from search results\n   801→- **Action**: User observes the FlightSummary section\n   802→- **Expected**: The itinerary displays both legs in order: Leg 1 (LAX → DFW) with its airline, flight number, departure/arrival times, terminal info, and duration; then a layover indicator showing layover duration and airport (e.g., \"2h 15m layover at DFW\"); then Leg 2 (DFW → JFK) with its details. The timeline visualization shows the full journey with the layover marked.\n   803→\n   804→#### Test: FlightSummary shows total duration and stops count\n   805→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   806→- **Initial state**: User selected a 1-stop flight with total duration 8h 45m\n   807→- **Action**: User observes the FlightSummary header area\n   808→- **Expected**: A summary line displays the total journey duration \"8h 45m\" and the number of stops \"1 stop\". For nonstop flights, it shows \"Nonstop\".\n   809→\n   810→#### Test: FlightSummary shows overnight arrival indicator\n   811→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   812→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight that arrives the next day (departs 11:00 PM, arrives 6:00 AM +1)\n   813→- **Action**: User observes the arrival time in FlightSummary\n   814→- **Expected**: The arrival time displays a \"+1\" indicator next to it, signaling the flight arrives the following day.\n   815→\n   816→#### Test: FlightSummary shows aircraft type and amenities\n   817→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   818→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight with aircraft_type \"Boeing 737-800\", has_wifi=true, has_power=true, has_entertainment=false\n   819→- **Action**: User observes the flight leg details in FlightSummary\n   820→- **Expected**: The aircraft type \"Boeing 737-800\" is displayed. Amenity icons are shown: Wi-Fi icon (present), power outlet icon (present). Entertainment icon is not shown or shown as unavailable.\n   821→\n   822→#### Test: FlightSummary shows baggage allowance\n   823→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   824→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight and the booking page is loaded\n   825→- **Action**: User observes the FlightSummary details\n   826→- **Expected**: Baggage allowance information is displayed for the selected cabin class (e.g., \"1 carry-on bag, 1 checked bag included\" for economy).\n   827→\n   828→### PriceBreakdown\n   829→\n   830→#### Test: PriceBreakdown displays base fare per passenger\n   831→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   832→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight for 1 adult in economy class, base fare $250, taxes $45\n   833→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   834→- **Expected**: The breakdown shows a line item \"Base fare\" with \"$250\" for 1 adult. The line item is labeled with the passenger type \"Adult × 1\".\n   835→\n   836→#### Test: PriceBreakdown displays taxes and fees\n   837→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   838→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight with taxes_cents = 4500\n   839→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   840→- **Expected**: A \"Taxes and fees\" line item shows \"$45.00\". The taxes are listed as a separate line from the base fare.\n   841→\n   842→#### Test: PriceBreakdown displays total price\n   843→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   844→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight with base fare $250 and taxes $45\n   845→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   846→- **Expected**: A prominently displayed \"Total\" line shows \"$295.00\". It is visually distinct (bold, larger font, or separated by a divider) from the individual line items.\n   847→\n   848→#### Test: PriceBreakdown shows per-passenger-type pricing for mixed group\n   849→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   850→- **Initial state**: User searched with 2 adults, 1 child, 1 infant and selected a flight\n   851→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   852→- **Expected**: The breakdown shows separate line items for each passenger type: \"Adult × 2\" with the per-adult base fare and subtotal, \"Child × 1\" with the child base fare, \"Infant × 1\" with the infant base fare. Taxes and fees are shown. The grand total sums all passengers.\n   853→\n   854→#### Test: PriceBreakdown updates for round-trip flights\n   855→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   856→- **Initial state**: User selected a round-trip flight (outbound + return)\n   857→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   858→- **Expected**: The breakdown includes pricing for both the outbound and return flights. The total reflects the combined cost of both directions plus all taxes and fees.\n   859→\n   860→#### Test: PriceBreakdown reflects selected cabin class pricing\n   861→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   862→- **Initial state**: User searched for Business class and selected a flight\n   863→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   864→- **Expected**: The cabin class \"Business\" is indicated in the breakdown. The base fare reflects the business class pricing (higher than economy). The total price matches the business class total_price_cents from the database.\n   865→\n   866→### PassengerForm\n   867→\n   868→#### Test: PassengerForm displays correct number of passenger forms\n   869→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   870→- **Initial state**: User searched with 2 adults and 1 child, then selected a flight\n   871→- **Action**: User observes the PassengerForm section\n   872→- **Expected**: Three separate passenger sub-forms are displayed, labeled \"Passenger 1 (Adult)\", \"Passenger 2 (Adult)\", and \"Passenger 3 (Child)\". Each form has fields for first name, last name, date of birth, and gender.\n   873→\n   874→#### Test: PassengerForm shows primary passenger contact fields\n   875→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   876→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded with 2 adults\n   877→- **Action**: User observes Passenger 1 form\n   878→- **Expected**: Passenger 1 (primary passenger) has additional fields for email address and phone number that are not present on the other passenger forms.\n   879→\n   880→#### Test: PassengerForm first name and last name input\n   881→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   882→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, passenger forms are empty\n   883→- **Action**: User types \"John\" in the first name field and \"Doe\" in the last name field of Passenger 1\n   884→- **Expected**: The first name field displays \"John\" and the last name field displays \"Doe\". The input is reflected in the form state.\n   885→\n   886→#### Test: PassengerForm date of birth picker\n   887→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   888→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   889→- **Action**: User clicks the date of birth field and selects a date (e.g., January 15, 1990)\n   890→- **Expected**: A date picker opens. After selecting the date, the field displays \"01/15/1990\" (or equivalent formatted date). The date picker closes.\n   891→\n   892→#### Test: PassengerForm gender dropdown\n   893→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   894→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   895→- **Action**: User clicks the gender dropdown\n   896→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens with options (e.g., \"Male\", \"Female\", \"Other\", \"Prefer not to say\"). Selecting an option updates the field and closes the dropdown.\n   897→\n   898→#### Test: PassengerForm email validation\n   899→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   900→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   901→- **Action**: User types \"invalid-email\" in the email field and attempts to submit\n   902→- **Expected**: A validation error appears on the email field indicating an invalid email format (e.g., \"Please enter a valid email address\"). The form does not submit.\n   903→\n   904→#### Test: PassengerForm email accepts valid input\n   905→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   906→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   907→- **Action**: User types \"john.doe@example.com\" in the email field\n   908→- **Expected**: The email field displays \"john.doe@example.com\" with no validation errors.\n   909→\n   910→#### Test: PassengerForm phone number input\n   911→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   912→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   913→- **Action**: User types \"+1 555-123-4567\" in the phone number field\n   914→- **Expected**: The phone number field accepts and displays the input. No validation error is shown.\n   915→\n   916→#### Test: PassengerForm required field validation\n   917→- **Components**: PassengerForm, BookingAction\n   918→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, all passenger forms are empty\n   919→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Book Flight\" button without filling in any fields\n   920→- **Expected**: Validation errors appear on all required fields (first name, last name, date of birth, gender for each passenger; email and phone for primary passenger). The booking is not submitted. Error messages indicate which fields are required.\n   921→\n   922→#### Test: PassengerForm infant passenger form\n   923→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   924→- **Initial state**: User searched with 1 adult, 1 infant and selected a flight\n   925→- **Action**: User observes the passenger forms\n   926→- **Expected**: Two forms are displayed: \"Passenger 1 (Adult)\" with contact fields, and \"Passenger 2 (Infant)\" with first name, last name, date of birth, and gender but no email/phone fields.\n   927→\n   928→#### Test: PassengerForm can be filled and edited multiple times\n   929→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   930→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, passenger form is empty\n   931→- **Action**: User fills in first name \"John\", then changes it to \"Jane\", interacts with date of birth picker, then returns to first name and changes it to \"Alex\"\n   932→- **Expected**: Each edit is correctly reflected in the form. The final state shows \"Alex\" in the first name field. Other fields retain their entered values between edits.\n   933→\n   934→### BookingAction\n   935→\n   936→#### Test: BookingAction displays \"Book Flight\" button\n   937→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   938→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded with flight selected\n   939→- **Action**: User observes the BookingAction section\n   940→- **Expected**: A prominent \"Book Flight\" button is displayed. The button text reads \"Book Flight\" and is styled as a primary action button (blue background, white text).\n   941→\n   942→#### Test: BookingAction successfully books a flight\n   943→- **Components**: BookingAction, PassengerForm, PriceBreakdown\n   944→- **Initial state**: All passenger forms are filled out correctly (Passenger 1: John Doe, john@example.com, +1 555-123-4567, DOB 1990-01-15, Male)\n   945→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Book Flight\" button\n   946→- **Expected**: The booking is saved to the database. A confirmation message is displayed with a unique booking reference number (e.g., \"Booking confirmed! Reference: ABC123\"). The bookings table has a new row with status \"confirmed\", the correct flight_id, session_id, cabin_class, and total_price_cents. The booking_passengers table has corresponding passenger records.\n   947→\n   948→#### Test: BookingAction shows booking reference number\n   949→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   950→- **Initial state**: User has just successfully booked a flight\n   951→- **Action**: User observes the confirmation\n   952→- **Expected**: A booking reference number is prominently displayed (e.g., \"Your booking reference: GF-ABC123\"). The reference is unique and can be used to identify the booking in the My Trips page.\n   953→\n   954→#### Test: BookingAction prevents double booking\n   955→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   956→- **Initial state**: User has just successfully booked a flight and sees the confirmation\n   957→- **Action**: User attempts to click \"Book Flight\" again (e.g., via browser back or re-clicking)\n   958→- **Expected**: The button is either disabled after successful booking, or the system prevents duplicate bookings. No second booking is created in the database.\n   959→\n   960→#### Test: BookingAction shows loading state during submission\n   961→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   962→- **Initial state**: All passenger forms filled, user clicks \"Book Flight\"\n   963→- **Action**: User observes the button during submission\n   964→- **Expected**: The button shows a loading indicator (spinner or \"Booking...\" text) while the request is being processed. The button is disabled during this time to prevent multiple clicks.\n   965→\n   966→#### Test: BookingAction booking appears in My Trips\n   967→- **Components**: BookingAction, TripCard\n   968→- **Initial state**: User has just successfully booked a flight (LAX → JFK, Mar 25, Delta DL100, $295)\n   969→- **Action**: User navigates to the My Trips page\n   970→- **Expected**: The \"Upcoming\" tab shows the newly booked trip with route \"LAX → JFK\", date \"Mar 25\", airline \"Delta\", status badge \"Confirmed\", price \"$295\", and the booking reference number.\n   971→\n   972→#### Test: BookingAction handles booking error gracefully\n   973→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   974→- **Initial state**: All passenger forms filled, but a network or server error occurs during booking\n   975→- **Action**: User clicks \"Book Flight\" and the request fails\n   976→- **Expected**: An error message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking failed. Please try again.\"). The form data is preserved so the user does not need to re-enter information. The \"Book Flight\" button becomes clickable again.\n   977→\n   978→## Page: My Trips\n   979→\n   980→### Components\n   981→- TripsTabs\n   982→- TripCard\n   983→- TrackedRouteCard\n   984→- CancelBookingModal\n   985→\n   986→### TripsTabs\n   987→\n   988→#### Test: TripsTabs displays three tabs\n   989→- **Components**: TripsTabs\n   990→- **Initial state**: User navigates to the My Trips page\n   991→- **Action**: User observes the tab bar at the top of the page\n   992→- **Expected**: Three tabs are displayed: \"Upcoming\", \"Past\", and \"Tracked\". The \"Upcoming\" tab is selected by default and visually highlighted (e.g., underline or bold text with primary color #1A73E8).\n   993→\n   994→#### Test: TripsTabs switches to Past tab\n   995→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TripCard\n   996→- **Initial state**: My Trips page loaded with \"Upcoming\" tab active, user has both upcoming and past bookings\n   997→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Past\" tab\n   998→- **Expected**: The \"Past\" tab becomes visually selected. The content area updates to show only trips with past departure dates (status \"Completed\" or \"Cancelled\"). Upcoming trips are no longer visible.\n   999→","numLines":500,"startLine":500,"totalLines":1414}}}
