o ambitious, so I need to consolidate the Explore section. I can combine the DestinationMap and DealsSection into one task at 17 points, then keep the FlexibleDatesGrid separate at 9 points, which gives me a more manageable workload.\n\nNow I'm thinking about how to structure this properly—the spec requires each task to have subtasks that map to individual tests, so I should organize the components by page and group related functionality together. I'm breaking down the Search page into logical chunks: the selector components, the input fields, and the supporting features like recent searches, then doing the same for Search Results.\n\nLooking at the full breakdown, I have 14 groups total, but I should see if I can consolidate further—particularly the date and airport components since they're both input-related, and maybe combine some of the smaller feature groups to reduce the overall number of tasks. I've settled on eight bundle groups that keep each under the token limit: selectors together at 14, passengers and search button at 16, airport autocomplete standalone at 11, dates with recent and popular searches at 20, results summary with price tracking at 14, filters as their own group at 17, flight cards with pagination at 20, and booking summary at 7.\n\nNow I'm adding the price breakdown to the booking summary for 13 total, then passenger form with booking action at 17, trips tabs with cards at 19, tracked routes with cancel modal at 14, destination map with deals at 17, and flexible dates grid at 9. That gives me 13 task groups to organize, but I'm realizing the spec actually wants all page tasks bundled together in a single call rather than split across multiple ones.\n\nI need to be more careful about the constraint that each spec file can only have 20 or fewer test calls, so pages exceeding that limit will need to be split into separate tasks. Let me rename the subtasks to follow a cleaner pattern and then write out the full add-task call.","signature":""}],